<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toggenburg War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1712</span> · Also known as Second War of Villmergen, Second Villmergen War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second War of Villmergen was a religious war of 1712 in the Old Swiss Confederacy, arising from a dispute in the Toggenburg between its Protestant subjects and the Prince-Abbot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-gallen">St. Gallen</a>. Zürich and Bern defeated the Catholic cantons at Villmergen on 25 July 1712, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-aarau-1712">Peace of Aarau</a> ended Catholic predominance in the common lordships.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toggenburg-war.jpg" alt="Toggenburg War" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sidonius · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Zweiter_Villmergerkrieg_1712.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
